	"system": {
		"description": {
			"value": "<p><em>With a fell incantation, you conjure a drifting cloud of putrid, yellow-green poisonous fog that seeps into creatures through their skin.</em></p><p><strong>[[/save constitution]]{Constitution Save}</strong></p><p>Creatures are affected even if they hold their breath or don't need to breathe.</p><ul><li><p><strong>Failure</strong> : Targets take [[/damage 5d8 poison]] damage and gain the &amp;reference[poisoned] condition. Targets roll again at end of their turns, ending the poisoned effect on success.</p></li><li><p><strong>Success</strong> : Half damage.</p></li><li><p><strong>Area Hazard</strong> : The area is &amp;reference[lightly obscured]. Targets roll a save when they enter or when they end their turn in the area (but only once per turn).</p></li><li><p><strong>&amp;reference[concentration]{Concentration}: </strong>At the start of each of your turns, you can choose to move the area of effect up to 10 ft in any direction.</p></li></ul><p><strong>*Upcasting:</strong> Increase damage by [[/damage 1d8 poison]]{1d8} for each spell level above 5th.</p><p><em>A moderate wind (at least 10 miles per hour) can move the cloud 10 ft. per round. A strong wind (at least 20 miles per hour) disperses the cloud and ends the spell.</em></p>",
			"chat": ""
		},
